<div id="post" class="clearfix">
	<div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-family: Lato;"><br /><br /><span style="font-size: 24px;"><strong>Upcoming Election Information<br /></strong><span style="font-size: 18px;">In person early voting and vote by mail will be available for all elections</span></span><br /><br /><img src="https://www.norfolkmass.gov/Document_Center/Departments/Town Clerk/Election Resources/Early hours Nov General.jpg?t=202609290932440" alt="Early hours Nov General" width="369" height="478" /><br /><br /><br />November 3, 2026 state general election <br />Click on the link for a look at the ballot:&nbsp; &nbsp;<a href= "https://www.norfolkmass.gov/Document_Center/Departments/Town Clerk/Election Resources/SAMPLE NOV 3 2026 BALLOT.pdf?t=202609241554100"  target="_blank"  >SAMPLE BALLOT</a><br /><br /><br />Click on the Information for Voters cover for a link to information on the ballot questions.<br /><br /><a href= "https://www.norfolkmass.gov/Document_Center/Departments/Town Clerk/Election Resources/2026 Ballot Question Information.pdf?t=202609221553580" style="width: 200px; height: 250px;"  target="_blank"  ><img src="https://www.norfolkmass.gov/Document_Center/Departments/Town Clerk/Election Resources/Red book.jpg?t=202609221553140" style="width: 200px; height: 265px;"  alt="Red book" height="262" /></a><br /></span></span></span>
<p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-family: Lato; font-size: 18px;"><br />You can also click here for the audio file of the information for voters book: <a rel="noopener" href="https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/download/research-and-statistics/MA-Info-For-Voters-2026.mp3" target="_blank" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.sec.state.ma.us/divisions/elections/download/research-and-statistics/MA-Info-For-Voters-2026.mp3&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1790708484747000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1Ef_rRaVeELgC9vJ4M4mq4">https://www.sec.state.ma.us/<wbr />divisions/elections/download/<wbr />research-and-statistics/MA-<wbr />Info-For-Voters-2026.mp3</a><br /><br /><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-family: Lato;">Additional information about voting in Norfolk can be found on the Election Resource page.</span></span><br /><br /><br /><img src="https://www.norfolkmass.gov/Document_Center/Departments/Town Clerk/Misc files/Pictures/Other/Town Clerks Office.jpg?t=202609241556390" alt="Town Clerks Office" width="456" height="280" /><br /><br />The Mission of the Town Clerk's office is to manage and preserve the official records of the Town of Norfolk; to assist the public in accessing public documents and information; to work hand in hand with other departments to provide excellence in service; to support the needs of the various Boards and Committees; to comply with and help facilitate state and local statutes; to administer honest and fair Elections. We strive to provide these services in a manner that is competent, efficient, fair, and courteous. The Town Clerk's duties and responsibilities are spelled out and governed by 73 chapters and 451 sections of Massachusetts General Laws, as well as Norfolk Town Bylaw.</span></p>
<div style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-family: Lato;">We welcome inquiries from all citizens seeking information or assistance.</span></span></div>
<span style="font-size: 18px;"><span style="font-family: Lato;"><br /><br /></span></span><br /><strong><span style="font-size: 18px;"><em><span style="font-family: Lato;"><br /></span></em></span></strong></div>
</div>


